 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Overfitting:** If the number of training views is small, the 2D neural renderer may overfit. This is mitigated by distillation: using a pre-trained NeRF to synthesize pseudo ground truth viewpoints by randomly sampling within the available viewing zone [S1].
+*   **Overfitting:** If the number of training views is small, the 2D neural renderer may overfit [S1]. This is mitigated by distillation: using a pre-trained NeRF to synthesize pseudo ground truth viewpoints by randomly sampling within the available viewing zone [S1].
 *   **Coordinate Rounding:** Simply rounding the reprojected coordinates $(\hat{u}, \hat{v})$ has a negligible impact on performance and is used for efficiency [S1].
-*   **No Perfect Motion Vectors:** Unlike game engines, NeRF does not provide high-precision motion vectors. The method relies on noisy depth maps from volume rendering, which requires the joint training of feature fields and the renderer to hallucinate high-fidelity details [S1].
